3. DDP validation collective failure fix
   - Failed log:
     - `checkpoints/train_nafnet_teacher_deploy_denoise_x1_width64_conservative_260521/resume_260526.log`
   - Symptom:
     - epoch 29 validation completed, then epoch 30 start failed with `RuntimeError: Invalid mt19937 state`.
     - NCCL watchdog showed rank mismatch: one rank entered RNG `BROADCAST`, the other was still in checkpoint/barrier-side collective work.
   - Root cause:
     - validation metrics were computed independently on each DDP rank.
     - only the rank whose local PSNR exceeded `best_metric_val` entered `save_checkpoint(is_best=True)`.
     - the other rank skipped best-checkpoint save and moved into the next epoch, so collective ordering diverged.
   - Code change:
     - `src/engine/trainer.py`
     - train loss and validation metrics are reduced across all ranks with `accelerator.reduce(...)`.
     - best checkpoint and early stopping decisions now use the same reduced metrics on every rank.
     - CSV, TensorBoard, and tqdm output are restricted to the main rank.
   - Verification:
     - host: `python3 -m py_compile src/engine/trainer.py tools/train.py`
     - container: `python3 -m py_compile src/engine/trainer.py tools/train.py`

4. Relaunch after fix
   - New log:
     - `checkpoints/train_nafnet_teacher_deploy_denoise_x1_width64_conservative_260521/resume_260526_after_rng_fix.log`
   - Relaunch command:
     - `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 accelerate launch --num_processes=2 tools/train.py --resume checkpoints/train_nafnet_teacher_deploy_denoise_x1_width64_conservative_260521/last.pth`
   - Resume checkpoint state:
     - `last.pth` was epoch 29 before relaunch.
     - resumed at epoch 30.
   - Post-fix evidence:
     - epoch 30 completed and saved.
     - epoch 31 completed and saved.
     - new `training_log.csv` rows after the fix are single main-rank rows instead of rank-duplicated rows.
     - no `Traceback`, `RuntimeError`, `Invalid mt19937`, `NCCL`, `FAILED`, or `timeout` string found in the new resume log at checkout check.

